Description: Give the Windows install mode its own identity, so Brumel does not
 share a profile, registry keys, file associations or COM registrations with an
 installed Chromium: user data under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Brumel, app and ProgIDs
 named Brumel, the brumel: launch scheme, and new GUIDs for Active Setup, the
 toast activator, the elevation service and the tracing service. COM interface
 IDs stay the same, because they belong to the IDL files and their pre-built
 MIDL output. The sandbox AppContainer SID prefix is unchanged on purpose
 (upstream value, so sandbox behavior is identical). install_static unit test
 expectations follow the new directory and app ID.
Origin: brumel
Module: branding
Feature: CORE-004
Upstreamable: no
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

